只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"🐳 DeepSeek Harness Desktop","id":"gh:1334714311","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"Minke","slug":"lencx/Minke","topics":["agent","ai-agents","codex","cordis","deekseek","desktop","dsh","dsh-plugin","harness","linux","macos","skills","windows"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"🐳 DeepSeek Harness Desktop"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"Minke"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A local-first desktop agent workspace powered by DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Minke brings conversations, files, terminals, and a shared browser into a local-first desktop agent "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"workspace powered by DeepSeek Harness. Available on macOS, Windows, and Linux, with sessions and set"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"tings stored on your computer."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> Minke is an independent community project under active development. Packaged releases may differ f"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"rom the current source."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Highlights"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **Shared browser control** — Watch the agent work in visible browser tabs, take over at any time, "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"and send annotated page context back to the conversation.\n- **One workspace** — Keep conversations, "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"files, and terminals side by side. Organize work with split views and a bottom panel; edit files, pr"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"eview documents, and review changes in place.\n- **Access across devices** — Reach your workspace thr"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"ough Web / PWA on a phone or another computer, or start tasks through WeChat, Telegram, and Discord."},{"id":"p8s6","text":"\n- **Cloud and local models** — Use cloud providers or custom endpoints, discover LM Studio and Olla"},{"id":"p8s7","text":"ma models, and optionally start local services.\n- **Agents and plugins** — Use DSH's presets, skills"},{"id":"p8s8","text":", subagents, and scheduled tasks, and extend the workspace through native plugin management."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Remote access from another device"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Minke remote access is a responsive Web client backed by Minke Host—not a\nvideo stream or touch-cont"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"rolled projection of the Electron window. From a\nphone you can continue conversations, start agent t"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"asks, manage project files,\nand use a terminal that runs on the Minke computer."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> **Tailscale Serve over HTTPS**, **Tailscale Direct IP**, and\n> **Cloudflare Access** hav"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"e all completed end-to-end regression testing and\n> are currently available."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- **Tailscale Serve over HTTPS (recommended)** — Best for devices already joined to the same tailnet"},{"id":"p12s2","text":". It provides a secure HTTPS address and supports PWA installation.\n- **Tailscale Direct IP (advance"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"d)** — Binds only to the current device's Tailscale IPv4. Traffic remains end-to-end encrypted by Ta"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ilscale, but the address uses HTTP and is not a browser secure context.\n- **Cloudflare Access** — Ex"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"poses a named tunnel protected by an identity policy, without requiring Tailscale on the phone. It r"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"equires a configured Cloudflare Tunnel, Access application, and an explicit allow policy."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Recommended setup: Tailscale Serve"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Minke can expose its Web UI privately through Tailscale Serve. It keeps Harness on the local loopbac"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"k address, does not bind it to the LAN, and does not enable the public Tailscale Funnel."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"1. Install Tailscale on the Minke computer and the phone, sign both into the\nsame tailnet, and confi"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"rm the computer is connected.\n2. In Minke, open **Connections → Device access → Remote access**, sel"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ect\n**HTTPS Serve**, and enable remote access. Minke connects in the\nbackground; no restart is requi"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"red.\n3. Copy or open the displayed\n`https://…ts.net` address on the phone."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Install as a PWA"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Open a Tailscale Serve or Cloudflare Access HTTPS address, choose\n**Install Minke** in the sidebar, "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"and accept the browser install prompt. On\niPhone or iPad, use **Share → Add to Home Screen**. The in"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"stalled app launches\nin standalone mode; when connectivity is poor it shows connection or offline\nfe"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"edback instead of silently presenting cached workspace content."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Minke activates only one remote route at a time, owns its foreground proxy\nwhile the app is running,"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" and stops it on exit. The remote page can start\nagent tasks and use local tools already authorized "},{"id":"p18s3","text":"in Minke, so grant access\nonly to trusted tailnet members or Cloudflare Access identities."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Download Minke only from the official GitHub Releases page. The links below always point to the late"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"y from the official GitHub Releases page. The links below always point to the latest stable release."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Platform | Architecture | Package |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| macOS | Apple Silicon (`arm64`) | Download `.dmg` |\n| macOS | Intel (`x64`) | Download `.dmg` |\n| "},{"id":"p22s2","text":"Windows | `x64` | Download `.exe` |\n| Linux | Debian / Ubuntu (`x64`) | Download `.deb` |\n| Linux | "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"Fedora / RHEL (`x64`) | Download `.rpm` |\n| Linux | `x64` (portable AppImage) | Download `.AppImage`"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"dora / RHEL (`x64`) | Download `.rpm` |\n| Linux | `x64` (portable AppImage) | Download `.AppImage` |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Release checksums are available in `SHA256SUMS`."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Packaged macOS, Windows, and Linux builds check for stable updates\nautomatically. Minke selects the "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"fixed DMG, EXE, DEB, RPM, or AppImage asset\nfor the running system, verifies the immutable GitHub Re"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"lease, URL chain,\nexact size, SHA-256 digest, and available OS provenance marker, then asks\nbefore o"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"pening it. Disable background downloads under\n**Settings → Minke → Preferences → Software updates** "},{"id":"p24s5","text":"to require a\n**Download update** confirmation first, or use **About Minke → Check for\nupdates** at a"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"ny time. Installation always remains explicit. See\ndesktop application updates for the user flow and"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"on always remains explicit. See\ndesktop application updates for the user flow and\nplatform behavior."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### macOS"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"1. Download the `.dmg` file and open it.\n2. Drag `Minke.app` into the Applications folder.\n3. Curren"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"t pre-release builds are not notarized. First try Apple's Open Anyway flow under **System Settings →"},{"id":"p26s3","text":" Privacy & Security**.\n4. If you explicitly accept the risk and the system flow is unavailable, remo"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"ve quarantine only from the exact installed app:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"5. Open Minke from the Applications folder."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"> [!CAUTION]\n> Removing the quarantine attribute bypasses a macOS security check. Minke's updater ne"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ver runs this command automatically. Use it only as a last resort for `Minke.app` downloaded from th"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"e official Releases page, and never replace the path with a broad directory."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"#### Authorize credential storage on macOS"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Minke requests Keychain access only after you open **Connections** and click\n**Authorize credential "},{"id":"p31s2","text":"access**. If macOS prompts, enter your Mac login\npassword and choose **Always Allow**. If access is "},{"id":"p31s3","text":"denied, click **Request\nauthorization again**."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"If credential storage remains unavailable, one possible cause is an invalid or\nmodified app signatur"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"e that prevents macOS from recognizing Minke's Keychain\nidentity. Verify the application:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"If verification fails for an older pre-release build that you trust and\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
